 "claim": "this unit-distance graph has circular chromatic number exactly 4: it is 4-colourable and not 3-colourable, and it admits no homomorphism to any circular clique K(p/q) with p/q < 4, checked against all 92 such ratios with denominator at most 12",
 "why_it_matters": "the Moser spindle is also 4-chromatic but has chi_c = 7/2, so it is half a colour loose.  A graph with chi_c = chi has no slack at its chromatic number, and this project's measurements say the palette caps that drive de Grey's construction live exactly where a carrier is tight in that sense.  This is the smallest tight example found here, reduced from Sa's 397 points by UNSAT-core extraction and then greedy deletion to vertex-minimality under single deletions.",
